at are the commodity trading times?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Trading hours depend on the specific asset and its underlying global exchange. For instance, spot gold and silver CFDs are available to trade roughly 23 hours a day, Monday through Friday. Energy contracts like WTI crude oil follow specific mercantile exchange schedules, generally running from Sunday evening to Friday afternoon. Check your trading panel for exact sessions.</p></div></details><details class="vr-faq-card"><summary>What can be traded in a commodities market?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Our commodities platform allows speculation on precious metals (such as gold, silver, and platinum) and energy products (like crude oil and natural gas). Using CFD contracts, you gain exposure to these global industrial markets with flexible leverage and low margin requirements, bypassing physical storage.</p></div></details><details class="vr-faq-card"><summary>How to trade gold?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Gold can be traded as spot CFDs (e.g. XAU/USD) which enable speculation on price trends without requiring physical bullion vaulting. To start, log into your trading account, select the gold ticker, analyze its trendline indicators alongside macroeconomic news (such as interest rate changes), and place your trade. Ensure you establish stop-loss controls to safeguard your balance.</p></div></details><details class="vr-faq-card"><summary>How to trade crude oil?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Trading crude oil is done by speculating on price changes using WTI or Brent Crude CFDs. Simply choose the specific oil contract in your trading platform and decide to open a buy (long) or sell (short) position. Given oil's high price volatility driven by OPEC+ policies and global storage reports, it is highly favored by intraday and momentum traders.</p></div></details><details class="vr-faq-card"><summary>What affects gold prices?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Gold valuations are typically driven by macroeconomic elements, including inflation trends, interest rate policies, Federal Reserve decisions, and the exchange rate of the US Dollar. Additionally, gold acts as a safe-haven asset, meaning geopolitical tensions and market uncertainty often trigger upward demand.</p></div></details><details class="vr-faq-card"><summary>Is commodity trading profitable?</summary><div class="vr-faq-content"><p style="font-size:15px;margin:0">Trading commodities can yield significant returns when paired with a disciplined strategy and thorough risk management. Highly liquid assets like gold and crude oil exhibit strong structural trends, offering frequent opportunities. However, because leverage boosts both gains and potential losses, proper risk controls are vital.</p></div></details></div></div></section><template data-va-step-active="0"><div class="vr-glassbox" style="padding:16px 20px;cursor:pointer;z-index:1;background:rgba(46,123,255,0.06);border-color:var(--accent);transition:all 0.2s ease;margin-left:0px" data-va-step-btn="0"><div class="vr-flex vr-ac" style="gap:16px"><div style="width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent-2);color:#05101F;display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:700;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace">1</div><div class="vr-flex vr-ac" style="justify-content:space-between;flex:1"><h4 style="font-size:17px;margin:0">Sign Up &amp; Verify</h4><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" style="transform:rotate(180deg);transition:transform 0.2s ease;opacity:0.7"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></div><div style="padding-left:48px;margin-top:10px"><p class="vr-muted" style="font-size:14.5px;margin:0;line-height:1.5">Create a live account and complete a quick KYC verification